== SECURITY item 12 full ==
12. **Remote Loan Notes do not carry the collateral release.** A Loan Note transfer (`nft_transfer` → `move_note`, contracts/nectar-core/src/notes.rs:332-349) sets `position.borrower` to the new owner, and repay is permissionless (`on_repay`, contracts/nectar-core/src/lib.rs:824). For collateral held on NEAR, a full repay releases the units to the current Note owner (lib.rs:852-858). For remote positions (Solana devnet, Base local fork), `request_remote_release` (contracts/nectar-core/src/remote.rs:957) signs the release to the **depositor recorded at deposit**, not to the Note owner, and the vault pays only that depositor (`withdraw`). A new owner who repays a remote loan therefore does not receive the collateral. The review's verifiers rejected this as a finding (documented behaviour, below); it is listed here so that nobody takes a remote Loan Note expecting the collateral.
== SECURITY item 11 full ==
11. **FACTS C-020, kept by decision: no Note transfer from the web app to a `0s` / `0u` account that does not exist yet.** The web app's Note-transfer receiver check (R2-09: `isImplicitAccount` in packages/sdk/src/network.ts, `receiverNeedsLookup` in packages/sdk/src/notes.ts) treats only 64-hex and `0x` + 40-hex ids as implicit (F-381). Deterministic `0s` and universal `0u` ids, which near-account-id 3.0.0 also calls implicit (F-382), take the `view_account` path. A missing account answers `UNKNOWN_ACCOUNT` (F-380), so Transfer stays off. This errs on the safe side: such a Note cannot be sent before the account exists, and nothing is stranded. Kunal kept the behaviour on 2026-11-11 (D-029). The contract does not check receivers; this is a web app and SDK rule, and a direct `nft_transfer` call is not affected.
